{"content_hash": "63e9daf3500fc9cd", "version_id": 413, "article_id": 42, "level_code": "en_b1", "lang": "en", "level": 3, "level_label": "B1 中级", "title": "Margaret Hamilton, who wrote the Apollo 11 software, dies at 90", "title_zh": "写出阿波罗11号软件的玛格丽特·汉密尔顿去世，享年90岁", "has_translation": true, "topic": "science", "source": "guardian_science", "source_url": "https://www.theguardian.com/science/2026/oct/07/margaret-hamilton-moon-computer-software", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1520908695049-da13395b27a6?ixid=M3wxMDk3Mzk1fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8MXx8bWFyZ2FyZXQlMjBoYW1pbHRvbnxlbnwwfDB8fHwxNzkxNTk0Mzc2fDA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&w=1600&q=75&fm=jpg&fit=max", "provider": "unsplash", "credit": "Photo by Keith Luke on Unsplash", "author": "Keith Luke", "credit_url": "https://unsplash.com/@lukephotography?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "source": "Unsplash", "source_url": "https://unsplash.com/photos/red-house-beside-body-of-water-with-white-motor-boats-during-daytime-Ad2BXIYc_gc?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "fallback": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(116, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(154, 46%, 48%)", "label": "SCIENCE", "seed": "1c94d1b8ff91"}}, "published_date": "2026-10-08", "word_count": 190, "reading_minutes": 0.9, "lead": "Margaret Hamilton was a computer pioneer. Her software helped Apollo 11 land on the moon in 1969. She has died at the age of 90.", "lead_zh": "玛格丽特·汉密尔顿是一位计算机先驱。她的软件在1969年帮助阿波罗11号登上月球。她去世了，享年90岁。", "preview": "MIT announced on Wednesday that Margaret Hamilton died on 30 September. She was 90 years old. In a time before the words 'software engineer'", "preview_zh": "麻省理工学院周三宣布，玛格丽特·汉密尔顿于9月30日去世，享年90岁。在“软件工程师”这个词还不常见的年代，她跟着一位著名的麻省理工学院气象学家学习编程。后来，她编写了能发现敌机的软件。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 403, "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/42/en_b1.mp3", "duration": 77.013, "size_bytes": 465840, "engine": "edge-tts", "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural", "word_count": 219, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@fc48a26/content/data/versions/413.json", "paragraphs": ["MIT announced on Wednesday that Margaret Hamilton died on 30 September. She was 90 years old. In a time before the words 'software engineer' were common, she learned to program from a famous MIT weather scientist. Later, she wrote software that could find enemy planes.", "When MIT got a NASA contract to build the Apollo flight software, Hamilton quickly joined the team. She said she loved the idea because it had never been done before. She was the first programmer to join and the first woman hired.", "In 1969, just minutes before Apollo 11 was going to land, an alarm rang on the onboard computer. The team had to decide whether to stop the mission. However, the spacecraft kept going because Hamilton's software was working perfectly.", "The software told everyone about a hardware problem and fixed it by restarting important tasks. In 2016, Barack Obama gave Hamilton the Presidential Medal of Freedom and mentioned this moment. She is survived by her family.", "Looking back in 2009, Hamilton said, 'We were the luckiest people in the world. There was no choice but to be pioneers, and no time to be beginners.'"], "paragraphs_zh": ["麻省理工学院周三宣布，玛格丽特·汉密尔顿于9月30日去世，享年90岁。在“软件工程师”这个词还不常见的年代，她跟着一位著名的麻省理工学院气象学家学习编程。后来，她编写了能发现敌机的软件。", "当麻省理工学院拿到NASA开发阿波罗飞行软件的合同时，汉密尔顿很快加入了团队。她说她喜欢这个想法，因为以前从来没有人做过。她是第一个加入的程序员，也是他们雇用的第一位女性。", "1969年，就在阿波罗11号即将登陆前几分钟，机载电脑响起了警报。团队必须决定是否中止任务。然而，飞船继续前进，因为汉密尔顿的软件运行得非常完美。", "软件告诉大家有一个硬件问题，并通过重启重要任务来解决它。2016年，巴拉克·奥巴马授予汉密尔顿总统自由勋章，并提到了这一时刻。她身后留下了家人。", "在2009年回顾时，汉密尔顿说：“我们是世界上最幸运的人。除了当先驱别无选择，也没有时间当初学者。”"], "body": "MIT announced on Wednesday that Margaret Hamilton died on 30 September. She was 90 years old. In a time before the words 'software engineer' were common, she learned to program from a famous MIT weather scientist. Later, she wrote software that could find enemy planes.\n\nWhen MIT got a NASA contract to build the Apollo flight software, Hamilton quickly joined the team. She said she loved the idea because it had never been done before. She was the first programmer to join and the first woman hired.\n\nIn 1969, just minutes before Apollo 11 was going to land, an alarm rang on the onboard computer. The team had to decide whether to stop the mission. However, the spacecraft kept going because Hamilton's software was working perfectly.\n\nThe software told everyone about a hardware problem and fixed it by restarting important tasks. In 2016, Barack Obama gave Hamilton the Presidential Medal of Freedom and mentioned this moment. She is survived by her family.\n\nLooking back in 2009, Hamilton said, 'We were the luckiest people in the world. There was no choice but to be pioneers, and no time to be beginners.'", "body_zh": "麻省理工学院周三宣布，玛格丽特·汉密尔顿于9月30日去世，享年90岁。在“软件工程师”这个词还不常见的年代，她跟着一位著名的麻省理工学院气象学家学习编程。后来，她编写了能发现敌机的软件。\n\n当麻省理工学院拿到NASA开发阿波罗飞行软件的合同时，汉密尔顿很快加入了团队。她说她喜欢这个想法，因为以前从来没有人做过。她是第一个加入的程序员，也是他们雇用的第一位女性。\n\n1969年，就在阿波罗11号即将登陆前几分钟，机载电脑响起了警报。团队必须决定是否中止任务。然而，飞船继续前进，因为汉密尔顿的软件运行得非常完美。\n\n软件告诉大家有一个硬件问题，并通过重启重要任务来解决它。2016年，巴拉克·奥巴马授予汉密尔顿总统自由勋章，并提到了这一时刻。她身后留下了家人。\n\n在2009年回顾时，汉密尔顿说：“我们是世界上最幸运的人。除了当先驱别无选择，也没有时间当初学者。”", "text": "MIT announced on Wednesday that Margaret Hamilton died on 30 September. She was 90 years old. In a time before the words 'software engineer' were common, she learned to program from a famous MIT weather scientist. Later, she wrote software that could find enemy planes. When MIT got a NASA contract to build the Apollo flight software, Hamilton quickly joined the team. She said she loved the idea because it had never been done before. She was the first programmer to join and the first woman hired. In 1969, just minutes before Apollo 11 was going to land, an alarm rang on the onboard computer. The team had to decide whether to stop the mission. However, the spacecraft kept going because Hamilton's software was working perfectly. The software told everyone about a hardware problem and fixed it by restarting important tasks. In 2016, Barack Obama gave Hamilton the Presidential Medal of Freedom and mentioned this moment. She is survived by her family. Looking back in 2009, Hamilton said, 'We were the luckiest people in the world. There was no choice but to be pioneers, and no time to be beginners.'", "vocab": [{"word": "pioneer", "pos": "noun", "zh": "先驱", "note": "指第一个做某事的人"}, {"word": "software", "pos": "noun", "zh": "软件", "note": "计算机程序"}, {"word": "announce", "pos": "verb", "zh": "宣布", "note": "正式告诉大家"}, {"word": "contract", "pos": "noun", "zh": "合同", "note": "正式的工作协议"}, {"word": "alarm", "pos": "noun", "zh": "警报", "note": "提醒危险的声音"}, {"word": "abort", "pos": "verb", "zh": "中止", "note": "停止正在进行的任务"}, {"word": "hardware", "pos": "noun", "zh": "硬件", "note": "计算机的物理部件"}, {"word": "compensate", "pos": "verb", "zh": "补偿", "note": "弥补问题"}, {"word": "survive", "pos": "verb", "zh": "幸存；比……活得长", "note": "这里指去世后家人还在"}, {"word": "reflect", "pos": "verb", "zh": "反思；回顾", "note": "认真思考过去的事"}], "title_original": "Margaret Hamilton, trailblazer whose software powered Apollo 11 moon landing, dies aged 90", "summary_original": "MIT computer scientist led development of software for moon mission and earned Presidential Medal of Freedom\nMargaret Hamilton, the computer pioneer whose software powered the first moon landing, has died, the Massachusetts Institute of Technology (MIT)\nannounced\non Wednesday. She was 90.\nIn an era before titles such as software engineer and computer scientist became mainstream, Hamilton, who died on 30 September, learned to program under the tutelage of a renowned MIT meteorologist.\nContinue reading...", "body_original": "Margaret Hamilton, trailblazer whose software powered Apollo 11 moon landing, dies aged 90\nMIT computer scientist led development of software for moon mission and earned Presidential Medal of Freedom\nMargaret Hamilton, the computer pioneer whose software powered the first moon landing, has died, the Massachusetts Institute of Technology (MIT)\nannounced\non Wednesday. She was 90.\nIn an era before titles such as software engineer and computer scientist became mainstream, Hamilton, who died on 30 September, learned to program under the tutelage of a renowned MIT meteorologist.\nShe continued to perfect the craft in an MIT laboratory, writing software that could detect enemy aircraft. When the institute received a Nasa contract to develop the Apollo onboard flight software, she jumped at the opportunity.\n“I was attracted both by the sheer idea and the fact that it had never been done before. I was the first programmer to join and the first woman they hired,” she\ntold\nthe Guardian in 2019.\nIn 1969, minutes before the\nApollo 11\nspacecraft was set to make history by landing on the lunar surface, an onboard computer’s alarm rang, indicating an emergency.\nFaced with a decision of whether to abort the mission, the spacecraft continued on. The software was working just as Hamilton and her team intended.\n“It quickly became clear the software was not only informing everyone that there was a hardware-related problem but was compensating for it – restarting and re-establishing the highest priority tasks. The error detection and recovery mechanisms had come to the rescue,” Hamilton said.\nBarack Obama referenced the incident when he presented her with the Presidential Medal of Freedom in 2016.\n“Our astronauts didn’t have much time, but thankfully they had Margaret Hamilton,” he said.\nHamilton is survived by her daughter, a son-in-law, two grandsons and four great-grandchildren,\naccording\nto MIT.\nReflecting on the mission, in a 2009\ninterview\nwith MIT News, Hamilton said: “Looking back, we were the luckiest people in the world; there was no choice but to be pioneers; no time to be beginners.”\nExplore more on these topics\nSpace\nApollo 11\nThe moon\nComputing\nnews\nShare\nReuse this content", "fetched_at": "2026-10-10T01:06:14.236394", "timeline": [{"i"